  "articleBody": "Replacing kitchen cabinets is a big undertaking, and it's easy to stumble if you're not careful. Here are some common mistakes and how to steer clear of them:<ul><li>**Incorrect Measurements:** This is a huge one! Failing to measure correctly can lead to ill-fitting cabinets and a lot of frustration. Double-check all your dimensions, especially tricky spots, or have a pro handle it.</li><li>**Overlooking Interfaces:** Don't forget how the new cabinets will interact with your existing flooring, countertops, and backsplash. These interfaces need to be carefully considered to avoid gaps or awkward transitions.</li><li>**Unclear Scope of Work:** Make sure you clarify exactly what's included in your quote. Is installation covered? What about trim, filler pieces, and decorative panels? Get it all in writing to prevent surprises.</li><li>**Choosing Unsuitable Materials:** Some materials look great but aren't durable enough for kitchen use. Always check the quality of materials, joinery, and hardware for longevity.</li><li>**Skipping a Walkthrough:** At the end, do a thorough final walkthrough with your installer. This is your chance to spot any defects or ask for adjustments before the project is officially wrapped up.</li></ul>By being mindful of these common issues, you can ensure a smoother cabinet replacement process. If you're feeling unsure, reaching out to a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can make all the difference, providing peace of mind and a quality outcome.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}